  "query_preview": "..\n\n - Meteorological Overview:\n\nToday an upper-level ridge briefly builds in over North-central, \nCentral, and Southwestern Montana. This will allow warm temperatures \nto persist with a few showers around. The showers will be primarily \nconfined to the Northern Rocky Mountain Front and will be\nprimarily snow. On Thursday there is an upper-level ridge over \nNorth- central, Central, and Southwestern Montana. However cold \nair will slide south from Canada and bring well-below seasonal \naverage temperatures to North-central Montana on Thursday. On \nThursday morning snow lingers in the East Glacier area. Everywhere\nelse on Thursday it will be mostly dry. On Friday the upper-level\nridge remains over North-central, Central, and Southwestern \nMontana. This will bring mostly dry weather to the area on Friday.\nOn Friday the cool air from Canada remains over North-central \nMontana which will keep below seasonal average temperatures in \nplace on Friday across North-central Montana.\n\nOn Saturday an upper-level trough begins to approach North-central, \nCentral, and Southwestern Montana. There will be warm air advection \ndue to southerly flow aloft which will warm temperatures up to near \nseasonal averages. Through the day on Saturday it will be mostly \ndry. Saturday evening through Monday an upper-level trough moves \nover North-central, Central, and Southwestern Montana. This will \nbring widespread precipitation to the area Saturday evening through \nMonday. This will keep cool (slightly below seasonal average) \ntemperatures for North-central, Central, and Southwestern Montana on \nSunday and Monday. Tuesday an upper-level ridge moves over North-\ncentral, Central, and Southwestern Montana this will allow \ntemperatures to warm up with mostly dry weather. -IG\n\n - Forecast Confidence & Scenarios:\n\nToday through Thursday morning along the higher elevations of the \nRocky Mountain Front there is a 50 - 70% chance for 6 inches of snow \nor greater. Today through Thursday morning at Marias Pass there is a \n50 - 70% chance for 2 inches of snow or greater. Wednesday afternoon \nthrough Thursday morning there is a 50% chance for one half inch \nper hour snowfall rates and a 20% chance for snowfall rates of one\ninch per hour. As a result a Winter Weather Advisory has been \nissued for the East Glacier Park area from 3 PM Wednesday through \n6 AM Thursday.\n\nConfidence is increasing that for next Wednesday through at least \nnext Friday there will be a strong upper-level ridge over North-\ncentral, Central, and Southwestern Montana. This would bring well-\nabove seasonal averages for temperatures with a period of dry \nweather for next Wednesday through Friday. -IG",
